2026-09-28 — K02i: constant comparison selection and imm12 validation.

The initial shape RED retains a constant in a general register instead of
selecting CMP-immediate. Full bits<32>/bits<64> comparisons now select the
existing unshifted imm12 form for a known operand in [0,4095]. Selecting the
left operand reverses the relation, not its logical truth: SLT/SLE become
GT/GE, ULT/ULE become HI/HS, and EQ/NE remain unchanged. Only already-evaluated
SSA operands move; source evaluation, guards, effects and block arguments do
not. Narrow/pair, pointer, dynamic and nonmatching constants retain old paths.

A separate malformed-MIR RED shows the validator accepting 4096 in the
unshifted imm12 form. Validation now rejects out-of-range operands, including
4097 and UINT64_MAX; assembler aliases do not widen the declared MIR format.

Five MIR tests and one CLI test PASS. The matrix covers 96 comparison shapes,
1056 exact EvoIR/MIR value comparisons, 24 nonmatching controls, a dynamic
control, branch fusion and three malformed operands. All 96 shapes assemble
for each Linux/Darwin target (192 combinations). The C fixture passes O0/O2
C-HIR, EvoIR and MIR execution, and native shape checks.

Fourteen sealed ARM64 executions PASS: six whole-program controls across
EvoCC/GCC14/Clang19 O0/O2, and eight crossed callers/callees. The first Clang
compile rejected five signedness warnings in the test's expected-value
comparisons under -Werror. Explicit unsigned expected-result casts fix the
fixture without weakening warnings; native-warning-red.log is retained.
Final pinned release produces the same six assembly byte streams as the
successfully tested preparation. Sealed image identity is verified before
and after, network disabled; no FP/ABI/source-profile change is involved.

Original KVM object replay, unchanged argv/source/config, 60s per-unit budget:
                                  before text     after text
  virt/kvm/kvm_main.o              157984          153936
  arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/pgtable.o       32324           31440
Data/BSS sizes do not change. CMP-immediate occurrences increase 214 -> 1446
and 47 -> 322. All four objects assemble and match the reference symbol names
and kinds. Installed objects/config/Image hash identically before and after.
Nothing is installed; smaller code is NOT a measured runtime speedup.
The active kernel still uses frozen compiler 65035621..., excluding this fix.
K02/K03 and final-current-compiler integration remain OPEN.

The final serial affected five-crate gate against 3d5cd72 has 1083 PASS,
zero FAIL, four historical ignored tests; Clippy -D warnings and fmt PASS.
An earlier gate had an E0463 doctest artifact-resolution failure while a
second build used the same target directory; its gate.log is retained,
and it is not counted as a successful gate. Final source stayed fixed for the
complete successful rerun. Rust/Cargo are the pinned 1.97.1, offline.

